      "version": "0.4.0",
      "date": "2026-10-17T14:09:50Z",
      "latest": false,
      "notesHtml": "<ul><li><strong>Run a whole collection.</strong> Click ▶ next to a collection, or open <em>Run collection</em>. Every request is sent once, in the order you choose, and you see which passed — and why the others didn't. Save the result as HTML, JUnit (for CI dashboards), or JSON.</li><li><strong>Pass values from one request to the next.</strong> The new <em>Save values</em> tab takes a value from an answer — like the id of a new order — as <code>{{orderId}}</code> for the requests after it. Works in collection runs and between Sends.</li><li><strong>Honest reports when you're blocked.</strong> If a server or its firewall refuses your load test (429 &quot;too many requests&quot;, 403), the report now says so plainly, shows when it started and at what load, and stops praising response times that were really just fast error replies. Peak requests per second and average users are now measured correctly — older reports are corrected when you open them.</li><li><strong>About and Check for updates.</strong> See your version, check for a new one, and open your data folder — from &quot;Version … · About&quot; at the bottom of the sidebar.</li><li><strong>Practice API:</strong> create an order (<code>POST /orders</code>) and fetch it (<code>GET /orders/{id}</code>) to try passing values safely.</li></ul>\n<p>Already on 0.3.0 or 0.3.1? The app updates itself (installer version) — just restart when it asks.</p>",
