      "notesHtml": "<ul><li><strong>Import from Postman and OpenAPI.</strong> Bring in Postman collections and environments, or OpenAPI 3 / Swagger 2 files (JSON or YAML). Folders, auth, bodies, and variables come along; anything that can't is listed first.</li><li><strong>Single-number tiles and section headings.</strong> Put one big number anywhere on a report, group charts under headings, and try the new <em>By topic</em> view (Speed, Reliability, Load). Eight more numbers to choose from, in the order you pick.</li><li><strong>Formatted email report.</strong> Copy a designed summary into Outlook or Gmail, or download an email draft (.eml) with the full report attached.</li><li><strong>Updates.</strong> The installed app now checks for new versions and offers to restart into them. (Portable and macOS show a download link.)</li><li><strong>Optional usage counts.</strong> The app asks once whether to share anonymous counts. Say no and nothing is sent. Details: <a href=\"https://apitestcenter.com/privacy.html\">https://apitestcenter.com/privacy.html</a></li><li><strong>macOS and Linux previews</strong> (when attached below). Not yet signed: on macOS, right-click the app and choose <em>Open</em> the first time.</li></ul>\n<p>Coming from 0.2.0? Download and install this version once; after that, updates arrive by themselves.</p>",
